      "question": "If the coefficients of $x^7$ and $x^8$ in $(2 + \\frac{x}{3})^n$ are equal, then $n$ is",
      "options": [
        "56",
        "55",
        "45",
        "15"
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "(b) 55",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$T_{r+1} = ^nC_r 2^{n-r} (x/3)^r$.",
        "Coeff of $x^7$: $^nC_7 2^{n-7} 3^{-7}$. Coeff of $x^8$: $^nC_8 2^{n-8} 3^{-8}$.",
        "$\\frac{^nC_8}{^nC_7} = \\frac{2^{n-7} 3^{-7}}{2^{n-8} 3^{-8}} = 2 \\cdot 3 = 6$.",
        "$\\frac{n-7}{8} = 6 \\implies n-7 = 48 \\implies n=55$."
      ]
    },
